# NoteSync cloud container config. Copy to deploy/loop.env, fill the 3 REQUIRED values,
# done. NEVER commit this file (it's gitignored). Full walkthrough: EC2-SETUP.md.

# ============================ REQUIRED (3 things) ============================

# 1. Claude subscription token — run `claude setup-token` (browser) and paste it. Reads ink on
#    your Max/Pro plan, no metered tokens. Expires ~1 year.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# 2. Your notes repos, as `subpath=HTTPS_URL` pairs, comma-separated — one per source folder you
#    mirror to the device. (The folder list is taken from these subpaths automatically.)
DOCS_REPOS=RealtimeMFG=https://github.com/you/realtimemfg.git,hq=https://github.com/you/hq.git

# 3. A GitHub fine-grained PAT with Contents: read+write on those repos. Used via a credential
#    helper — never stored in a URL or log. If all repos are under ONE owner, set GITHUB_TOKEN.
#    If they span owners (fine-grained PATs are owner-scoped), use GITHUB_TOKENS instead:
#    one token per owner, "owner:token,owner:token".
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_TOKENS=your-user:github_pat_xxx,your-org:github_pat_yyy

# (Plus one file, not a variable: a Google Drive rclone.conf, mounted by docker-compose.)

# ============================ OPTIONAL (defaults shown) ======================
# RUN_MODE=loop               # loop = self-scheduled; oneshot = one pass then exit (cron/heartbeat)
# LOOP_INTERVAL=300           # seconds between passes in loop mode
# RCLONE_REMOTE=gdrive        # the rclone remote's name in rclone.conf
# DRIVE_PATH=Supernote        # your Supernote folder's name in Drive
# HEARTBEAT_STALE_SECS=300    # cloud defers while the laptop's been active within this; 0 = always run
# SUPERNOTE_SCAN_ROOTS=...    # auto-derived from the DOCS_REPOS subpaths; set only to override
# GIT_USER_NAME=NoteSync
# GIT_USER_EMAIL=NoteSync@localhost
